* SL_NEED
* Screen library: is the window as big as a full-screen program is laid out for?
* Copyright (c) 2026, SD Core for Linux.  This program is free software; you can redistribute
* it and/or modify it under the terms of the GNU General Public License, version 3 or later.
*
* START-HISTORY:
* 18 Oct 26 dm  New (terminal 140 by 42, phase 2).  One check and one message (12202) for every full-screen program of SD's
*               own, so that the size they insist on is stated in one place: SED now; the IDE and CED when their phase comes.
* 18 Oct 26 dm  Phase 3: the IDE and CED ask too; the fifth argument is for the debugger, which does without its full-screen
*               display instead of refusing (message 12607).
* 18 Oct 26 dm  Messages 12491 to 12493 became 12605 to 12607: 12485 to 12494 is the net slice's block (test-net-units W14).
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call $sl_need(name, minw, minh, msg, fallback)
*
*     name        what the program is called in the message (SED)
*     minw minh   the size the program is laid out for
*     msg         returned: null when the window ($sl_window) is at least that big; else message 12202, "SED needs a window of
*                 at least 140 columns by 42 lines; this one is 100 by 30".  The program prints it (or STOPs with it) and does
*                 not start.
*     fallback    1 for a program that does not refuse but does without (the debugger's full-screen display): the message is
*                 12607, "the debugger's full-screen display needs a window of at least 140 columns by 42 lines; this one is
*                 100 by 30, so it is using line mode".  Null for a program that refuses.
*
*   Only a program that is laid out for a size asks.  A user's SCREEN OPEN program asks for its own with MINSIZE w,h, and SD does
*   not impose 140 by 42 on it; the debugger's full-screen display falls back to line mode instead of refusing.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine sl_need(name, minw, minh, msg, fallback)
$catalog $sl_need

   call $sl_window(w, h)
   msg = ''
   if w < minw or h < minh then
      if fallback # '' and fallback # 0 then
         msg = sysmsg(12607, name, minw, minh, w : ' by ' : h)    ;* %1 needs a window of at least %2 by %3 for its full-screen display; ... %4 ...
      end else
         msg = sysmsg(12202, name, minw, minh, w : ' by ' : h)    ;* %1 needs a window of at least %2 columns by %3 lines; this one is %4
      end
   end

   return
end

* END-CODE
